For there to exist such an abelian subscheme, it is necessary and sufficient that it exist after every base change ⟦0⟧, where ⟦1⟧ is local Artinian;
if ⟦2⟧ is the spectrum of a local ring, it even suffices to test with the ⟦3⟧ where ⟦4⟧.
If ⟦5⟧ is reduced, then it equally suffices to test with the ⟦6⟧ that are the spectrum of a discrete valuation ring (complete, with algebraically closed residue field, if one desires).
